# Security headers for the static app (PROG-65).
#
# The Worker only runs for `/api/*` and the `/ph/*` analytics proxy
# (wrangler.jsonc `run_worker_first`), so the SPA document, JS, CSS, fonts, and
# icons are served straight from Cloudflare's asset handler — the Worker can't
# add headers to them. This `_headers` file is
# how Cloudflare static assets attach response headers; Vite copies `public/*`
# to the asset root, so it ships as `/_headers`. API responses get their own
# headers from a Worker middleware (src/worker/index.ts); the two are
# complementary, not redundant.
#
# CSP is tuned to exactly what the built `index.html` loads (verified PROG-65):
#   - script-src 'self'        — one external module bundle, plus exactly one
#                                pinned inline script (below), no blanket
#                                'unsafe-inline';
#     + 'sha256-yemgn44ZhCXv3NlHLmLLKNNwakGN+bLpBCd/mPlKShE=' — the PROG-150
#                                no-flash theme-boot script in index.html's
#                                <head> (sets data-theme from localStorage
#                                before first paint, so switching presets never
#                                flashes porcelain first). Hashed rather than
#                                'unsafe-inline'd to keep the policy pinned to
#                                this exact script; regenerate the hash (see
#                                that script's comment) if its text changes —
#                                the CSP will otherwise silently block it.
#     + static.cloudflareinsights.com — Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon, edge-
#                                injected into the HTML on the bck.dev zone.
#   - style-src 'unsafe-inline'— React/dnd-kit set inline `style` attributes
#                                (drag transforms, dynamic colors).
#   - font-src 'self' + data:  — fonts are self-hosted under /fonts
#                                (PROG-147); data: for any inlined glyph.
#   - img-src 'self' data: blob:— uploaded images are same-origin (/api/images);
#                                data:/blob: cover pasted-image previews.
#   - connect-src 'self'       — the client only ever fetches its own origin:
#                                /api, plus the /ph PostHog proxy (PROG-137),
#                                which exists precisely to keep PostHog first-
#                                party rather than on this allowlist;
#     + cloudflareinsights.com — the Web Analytics beacon POSTs RUM data there.
#   - frame-ancestors 'none'   — clickjacking defense (superset of X-Frame-Options).
# Sign-in is a top-level link to Google (not a form), so form-action 'self' is safe.
# Deliberately still blocked: Bot Fight Mode's edge-injected inline challenge
# script — it embeds a per-response timestamp, so it can only be allowed via
# 'unsafe-inline', which would gut the policy. Its console error is harmless;
# disable Bot Fight Mode (or its JavaScript Detections) on the zone to silence it.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-yemgn44ZhCXv3NlHLmLLKNNwakGN+bLpBCd/mPlKShE=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; manifest-src 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
